laurel 2012: the boot CPU may be Silver 0x0 (UEFI/DarwinBoot path) as well as Gold 0x100 (topaz shim path).

Mu-Silicium UEFI and DarwinBoot run on the core the ABL started, Kryo 260 Silver CPU0 (MPIDR 0x0, Cortex-A53
class, no 16K granule). The TOPAZ_4K kernel (4 KiB pages, topaz 0140/0141) runs on both clusters, so no hand-off
to a Gold core is needed; the ADT marks the running core (scripts/laurel/mkadt.py --boot silver: Silver cluster
first = E cluster 0, Gold = P cluster 1, like Apple SoCs whose cpu0 is an E core). topaz 0082 demanded MPIDR 0x100
because its 16K kernel cannot run on Silver; that stays for a 16K build. Decision and reasons:
docs/laurel_sprout/uefi-boot.md "Boot CPU".

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
@@ -149,11 +149,24 @@
 	/*
 	 * topaz: the ADT lists only the A73 (gold) cores and the shim boots xnu
 	 * on gold CPU 0x100 (the silver cluster has no 16K granule).
+	 * laurel 2012: under TOPAZ_4K (4 KiB pages, both clusters) UEFI/DarwinBoot
+	 * boots xnu on the ABL's core, Silver 0x0; the ADT marks it "running" and
+	 * lists it first. A 16K kernel still needs Gold 0x100.
 	 */
+#if defined(TOPAZ_4K)
+	if (topology->boot_cpu->cpu_id != 0 ||
+	    (topology->boot_cpu->phys_id != 0x100 && topology->boot_cpu->phys_id != 0x0)) {
+		panic("SWEET CPU: expected boot MPIDR 0x0 or 0x100 and logical CPU 0, got 0x%x/%u",
+		    topology->boot_cpu->phys_id, topology->boot_cpu->cpu_id);
+	}
+	IOLog("LAUREL CPU: boot cpu mpidr=0x%x (%s)\n", topology->boot_cpu->phys_id,
+	    topology->boot_cpu->phys_id == 0x100 ? "Gold, shim path" : "Silver, UEFI path");
+#else
 	if (topology->boot_cpu->cpu_id != 0 || topology->boot_cpu->phys_id != 0x100) {
 		panic("SWEET CPU: expected boot MPIDR 0x100 and logical CPU 0, got 0x%x/%u",
 		    topology->boot_cpu->phys_id, topology->boot_cpu->cpu_id);
 	}
+#endif
